      "content": "Certainly! One criticism is that these 15-minute cities often lead to gentrification, displacing lower-income residents and changing the cultural fabric of existing neighborhoods. Another argument is that while promoting local economies, such cities might inadvertently create inequalities, as not all residents can afford the real estate tax increases often associated with these developments. Critics also argue that the concept may be overly idealistic, assuming constant demand for diverse local services which might not be realistically sustainable financially. Lastly, there is a concern that the focus on reducing travel times within cities might neglect broader issues of urban sprawl and environmental sustainability.",
